$CATEGORY: VBS CSA / Section 1 - Customer Success Fundamentals

::Q1 - Primary Goal of CS::What is the primary goal of Customer Success? {
=Ensure customers achieve desired outcomes and receive value.
~Resolve only customer complaints.
~Increase internal meetings.
~Manage only invoices.
}

::Q2 - Purpose of Health Score::What is the purpose of a Customer Health Score? {
=Identify customer status, risks, and opportunities.
~Measure employee performance.
~Track marketing campaigns.
~Replace customer conversations.
}

::Q3 - CS vs Support::What best distinguishes Customer Success from Customer Support? {
=Customer Success is proactive and outcome-focused; Support is typically reactive and issue-focused.
~Customer Success only handles billing questions.
~Customer Success and Customer Support are the same function.
~Customer Success has no contact with customers.
}

$CATEGORY: VBS CSA / Section 2 - Customer Lifecycle Management

::Q4 - Renewal Timing::When should a CSM start renewal conversations? {
=Throughout the customer lifecycle.
~Only after the contract expires.
~Near the final day.
~Only when sales asks.
}

::Q5 - Purpose of a Playbook::What is the purpose of a customer playbook? {
=Provide guidance for repeatable customer situations.
~Store invoices.
~Replace CRM.
~Track attendance.
}

::Q6 - Renewal Readiness Trigger::Per the Renewal Management SOP, how many days before the renewal date should readiness assessment begin? {
=120 days
~10 days
~365 days
~It should not begin until the contract expires
}

$CATEGORY: VBS CSA / Section 3 - Customer Operations

::Q7 - Why SOPs Matter::Why are SOPs important? {
=They create consistent execution.
~They eliminate customer interaction.
~They replace CSM judgment.
~They are only for new employees.
}

::Q8 - Escalation First Step::Per the Escalation Management SOP, what is the required response time to acknowledge a customer escalation? {
=Within 2 business hours.
~Within 2 business days.
~Only after the issue is resolved.
~There is no defined response time.
}

::Q9 - Health Score RAG Thresholds::Using the VBS Health Scorecard RAG framework, a total score of 20 out of 35 classifies the account as: {
=🟡 Yellow — At Risk
~🟢 Green — Healthy
~🔴 Red — Critical
~The account cannot be classified without additional data
}

$CATEGORY: VBS CSA / Section 4 - Strategic Skills & Growth

::Q10 - Upsell Precondition::Before raising an upsell opportunity with a customer, what must be confirmed first? {
=The account's health status is 🟢 Green.
~The customer's contract is about to expire.
~The CSM's quota for the quarter.
~That the customer has never made a complaint.
}

::Q11 - Renewal vs Upsell Playbook::A customer's contract is expiring in 90 days and health is 🟡 Yellow. What is the correct first action? {
=Activate the At-Risk Customer Playbook before proceeding with renewal conversations.
~Immediately send the Renewal Discussion email.
~Introduce an upsell opportunity to strengthen the relationship.
~Wait until the health status changes on its own.
}

$CATEGORY: VBS CSA / Section 5 - AI & Modern CSM Skills

::Q12 - AI-Generated Content::What is the correct approach to AI-generated content? {
=Always verify and apply human judgment.
~Send immediately without review.
~Let AI make customer decisions.
~Avoid reviewing outputs.
}

$CATEGORY: VBS CSA / Practical Assessment (Manually Graded)

::Practical Case Study - Architecture Firm Account Recovery::[html]<p><strong>Scenario:</strong> You are the CSM for a customer who has worked with VBS for 8 months on BIM modeling services. You observe: reduced project activity, no new project request in 45 days, a missed scheduled review meeting, delayed feedback on a prior delivery, and an overdue invoice payment.</p><p><strong>Complete the following:</strong></p><ol><li>Assess current health status (🟢/🟡/🔴) and explain your reasoning.</li><li>Identify relationship, delivery, financial, and retention risks.</li><li>Create a prioritized action plan with owners and timelines.</li><li>Draft a professional outreach email to the customer.</li><li>Write the CRM note you would log for this account.</li></ol><p><em>Evaluation weighting: Problem Analysis 25%, Customer Communication 25%, Action Planning 25%, CRM Documentation 25%. Passing requires demonstrating proactive risk identification and professional, non-sales-pressured communication.</em></p> {}

::CSM Simulation Exercise - Delivery Timeline Complaint::[html]<p>A customer contacts you saying: <em>"We are not happy with the recent delivery timeline and are considering other options."</em></p><p>Describe your immediate response (how you would acknowledge the concern), your internal next steps, and how you would follow up with the customer.</p> {}
